# Code owners

# Default owner for everything. Taken from the authenticated GitHub account, not guessed
# from a directory name -- a CODEOWNERS rule pointing at a real person who is not the owner
# routes review to a stranger, which is worse than having no rule at all.
*                       @tecruz

# The paths below are where a mistake reaches past code review. They are listed so the next
# person to add an owner knows where the second pair of eyes is needed; the default above
# already covers them until then.
#
# packages/core/       exec shim handling, the JSON envelope contract
# packages/providers/  the gh transport, the local provider
# packages/worktrees/  claim/release/crew state machines
# packages/derive/     staging lifecycle, the write path
# packages/playbooks/  data: every URL is hand-maintained
#
# An agent's own pull requests should not be self-reviewed. That needs a second owner, so
# add one here when there is a second person: /.*copilot.*/  @tecruz @second-owner
